{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Sha'afu</b> — the meaning is like <i>male'ig</i> (scoffer). Why do my enemies <b>sha'afu</b> all day, when I have many angels on high fighting for my sake?! For the word <i>milkhamah</i> followed by a lamed indicates aid, for the meaning is 'for his sake,' as in <b>ha-nilcham lakhem</b>; only with the word <i>'im</i> is it pejorative."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:58.191170637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}